Fair enough.  Let me be more explicit.  If a fine is due and is not
voluntarily presented, the court should be able to auction any and all
victim assets in order to get the money due.  Disallowing the
auctioning of certain assets is equivalent to lowering fines due for
people with certain kinds of assets.  If this is what the law wants,
it should just set the fine explicitly based on such criteria.  I
suspect, though, that law customers would rather define such fine
reductions in terms of each party's general risk aversion, rather than
